  <diagram name="Scope and Findings" id="yljNZu_ZwGg2yEmICNAP">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1439" dy="817" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=24;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#183c43;align=left;" value="Week 5 | Scope and Findings" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1070" x="45" y="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="scope" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;1 · Process scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Akyba Mallett&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Purpose: Map the current&amp;nbsp; Cedar Junction appointment workflow from initial booking request to Intake check-in and handoff.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Start &amp;amp; End: Begins when a Visitor requests an appointment (portal or phone) (W05-S01) and ends when Intake routes the visitor to the Next staff team (W05-S03).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Roles: Visitor, Scheduling (Mateo Silva), Clinical Operations (Dr. Lena Okafor), Intake (Dana Ruiz), and Next staff team.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Out of Scope: Clinical care delivery after handoff, future software redesigns (W05-S02), and exposing clinical details across minimum-access boundaries&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt; (W04-S04).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="1085" x="45" y="65" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="walkthrough" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;2 · Check the two paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;Ordinary Path: Visitor requests appointment &amp;gt;Scheduling records preferences (W04-S03), holds slot, and sends booking confirmation (W05-S01) &amp;gt; Clinical Operations checks room/clinician and records readiness (W05-S02) &amp;gt; Visitor arrives &amp;gt; Intake sees &quot;Ready,&quot; confirms support, and routes visitor (W05-S03).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;Incident Path (W05-S04): Booking confirmed&amp;gt; Visitor arrives&amp;gt;Intake still sees &quot;Held&quot; &amp;gt; Intake manually contacts Scheduling and Clinical Ops to clear the block before routing.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;Gap &amp;amp; Limits: Booking confirmation is separate from readiness (W05-S01), and no readiness decision reached Intake before arrival (W05-S04). The records cannot prove why the decision was missing or how long the visitor waited.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="40" y="235" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;3 · Evidence and model review&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Sources: W05-S01–W05-S04, W04-S02–W04-S04.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Correction: Marked the readiness handoff to Intake as a dashed unresolved line instead of inventing a step.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Uncertainty: Why readiness never reached Intake and exact wait time (W05-S04); requires system logs and confirmation from Dr. Okafor and Mateo Silva.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="reflection" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;4 · Learning reflection (reuse your Discord paragraph)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Mapping this process made it clearer that Scheduling&#39;s booking confirmation (W05-S01) is separate from Clinical Operations&#39; readiness decision (W05-S02). The handoff to Intake is unclear because the incident trace (W05-S04) shows no readiness decision reaching Intake before arrival, forcing Dana Ruiz into a manual review with unrecorded wait time. Unlike Week 4&#39;s system rules and access boundaries (W04-S04), Week 5 captures how work happens today including bottlenecks and missing evidence without inventing steps.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="50" y="510" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
